---
layout: null
permalink: /feed/issues.xml
---
{%- comment -%}
  The edition feed: one entry per issue, hand-written rather than handed to
  jekyll-feed.

  jekyll-feed can emit a feed for any collection, and for front_pages it gets
  three things wrong. It dates every entry from site.time, because collection
  documents carry no `date` — so each deploy would re-date every issue and
  resurface old editions as new. It titles the feed "The Belvidere Wire |
  Front_pages", with no hook to override. And it dumps the whole rendered front
  page into each entry, about 9KB of it, which is the same twelve briefs the
  wire feed already carried as full dispatches.

  So: `generated` is the real publication stamp, and an entry is a digest —
  the lead headline in the title, the rest listed under it. Someone who wants
  the text subscribes to the wire; this is for someone who wants the edition.

  The headline list is read back out of the issue's own rendered HTML, which
  couples this template to the markup frontpage._brief_html emits. That is the
  trade for the list working on every issue ever published, including ones on
  disk before this feed existed, with no migration and no second copy of the
  headlines in front matter. If that markup changes, the guard below drops the
  list rather than emitting nonsense — check here when it does.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign issues = site.front_pages | sort: "issue" | reverse -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"{% if site.lang %} xml:lang="{{ site.lang }}"{% endif %}>
  <generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="{{ jekyll.version }}">Jekyll</generator>
  <link href="{{ page.url | absolute_url }}" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" />
  <link href="{{ '/issues/' | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" />
  <title type="html">{{ site.title | append: " | Editions" | xml_escape }}</title>
  <subtitle>One entry per edition of The Belvidere Wire — the briefs it led with, in the order it ran them. For every dispatch as it is filed, subscribe to the wire instead.</subtitle>
  {%- comment -%}
    Dated from the newest issue, not site.time: a rebuild that publishes
    nothing new should not tell every reader the feed has changed.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <updated>{% if issues.size > 0 %}{{ issues[0].generated | date_to_xmlschema }}{% else %}{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}{% endif %}</updated>
  <id>{{ page.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</id>
  <author><name>{{ site.author | xml_escape }}</name></author>
  {%- for issue in issues limit: 50 %}
  <entry>
    <title type="html">No. {{ issue.issue }}{% if issue.lead %} — {{ issue.lead | strip_html | xml_escape }}{% endif %}</title>
    <link href="{{ issue.url | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" />
    <published>{{ issue.generated | date_to_xmlschema }}</published>
    <updated>{{ issue.generated | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
    <id>{{ issue.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</id>
    {%- assign chunks = issue.content | split: '<h2 class="brief-headline">' -%}
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>{{ issue.brief_count }} brief{% if issue.brief_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}, filed {{ issue.generated | date: "%B %-d, %Y" }}.</p>
    {%- if chunks.size > 1 -%}
    <ol>
      {%- for chunk in chunks offset: 1 -%}
      {%- assign headline = chunk | split: '</h2>' | first | strip_html | strip -%}
      {%- assign parts = chunk | split: '"' -%}
      <li><a href="{{ parts[1] | prepend: site.url }}">{{ headline }}</a></li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
    {%- endif -%}
    <p><a href="{{ issue.url | absolute_url }}">Read edition No. {{ issue.issue }}</a></p>]]></content>
  </entry>
  {%- endfor %}
</feed>
